Minato's patch to frameworks/base's core/java/android/widget/RemoteViews.java at android-15.0.0_r1 (Apache-2.0),
framework breadth F4c: without RemoteCompose's player.

Why: RemoteViews names RemoteComposePlayer, RemoteComposeDocument and Theme in four places, for draw instructions that
a host sends when the feature flag drawDataParcel is on (Android 15 ships it off): `root instanceof
RemoteComposePlayer` in SetOnClickResponse's and the draw-instructions action's apply, `new RemoteComposePlayer` when
inflating, and `v instanceof RemoteComposePlayer` in performApply. The player is a compile-only stub in Minato, so the
instanceof of apply and reapply of any RemoteViews ended in a NoClassDefFoundError. The four places go: draw
instructions are not drawn, and every layout is inflated; nothing else changes.

